  "caption": "Quinn tweaked a knee chasing the bus, then stood at the open freezer while the group chat offered 17 opinions. So Quinn iced it for an hour, then another.\n\nIce can give short-term pain relief but doesn't speed up healing, and heat is mainly for comfort with stiffness.\n\nWhat can help: ice for 10–15 minutes wrapped in a cloth in the first few days, heat for stiffness or before exercise, gentle movement early on, protecting your skin, and putting most of your effort into graded loading.\n\nGet it checked if you can't put weight on it, swelling increases quickly, the area looks deformed, there's numbness, or your calf is painful, warm and swollen.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
